      "date": "2026-10-05 06:25:06.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(4 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nThe change itself is correct: `lnetctl net show --bogus` now exits non-zero (-EINVAL propagates through cfs_parser() to main()). Comments inline are about scope and the commit message. A small sanity-lnet check such as `do_lnetctl net show --bogus && error \"should fail\"` would keep this from regressing silently again, since the original problem was a test passing when it should not have.",
